# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# All `VITE_*` variables are bundled into the client at build time, so they
# must be safe to expose. Never put secrets here that the browser shouldn't see.

# =============================================================================
# Required — Supabase project credentials
# =============================================================================
#
# Where to find these:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com/dashboard
#   2. Settings -> API
#   3. Copy "Project URL"        -> used as the *upstream* origin only
#   4. Copy "anon public" or "publishable" key -> VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# Either the legacy JWT anon key or the newer sb_publishable_... key works.
# The client key is safe to expose — Row Level Security policies (in
# supabase/migrations/) restrict every table to the authenticated user.
# Never commit the `service_role` / secret key; it bypasses RLS.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mainland China / Cloudflare Pages (required for https://20270227.xyz)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Browsers in mainland China often cannot reach *.supabase.co (Failed to fetch).
# Do NOT point the client at the raw project URL in production. Proxy via the
# app domain so the browser only talks to 20270227.xyz:
#
#   Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables → Production:
#     VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://20270227.xyz/supabase
#     VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...   (publishable/anon key only)
#
#   Then trigger a new Pages deploy (Vite inlines VITE_* at build time).
#
# `/supabase` (same-origin path) also works and is resolved against the current
# host — useful for `pnpm dev` / `pnpm preview` with the Vite proxy:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=/supabase
#
# Optional server-only override for the Pages Function / Vite proxy target
# (not bundled; defaults to this project's supabase.co origin):
#   SUPABASE_UPSTREAM_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Production (Cloudflare Pages):
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://20270227.xyz/supabase
#
# Local Vite (proxies /supabase → SUPABASE_UPSTREAM_URL):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=/supabase
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-or-publishable-key

# =============================================================================
# Optional — branding / data controller identity (PIPL / GDPR)
# =============================================================================
#
# Shown on /privacy. Falls back to Chinese placeholders when unset, but you
# should fill these in before going to production so users know who is
# processing their data.

# VITE_DATA_CONTROLLER_NAME="经期记录运营者"
# VITE_DATA_CONTROLLER_EMAIL=privacy@your-domain.example
# VITE_PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL=https://your-domain.example/privacy

# =============================================================================
# Optional — push notifications (Web Push, Phase 4 Track C)
# =============================================================================
#
# Generate a VAPID keypair with:
#   node scripts/generate-vapid.mjs
# The public key is bundled into the client; the private key stays in
# Supabase Edge Function secrets (never committed). Never put
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or SEND_PUSH_CRON_SECRET in a VITE_* variable.

# VITE_PUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BPaste-public-key-here
#
# Edge Function secrets (supabase secrets set — server only):
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   exact match used by send-push
#   SEND_PUSH_CRON_SECRET       optional dedicated cron bearer
#   SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET         optional; verifies HS256 service_role JWTs
#   PUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY / PUSH_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY / PUSH_VAPID_SUBJECT

# =============================================================================
# Optional — Cloudflare Turnstile captcha (Phase 4 Track E)
# =============================================================================
#
# If unset, signup works without captcha. Once set, signup requires a
# Turnstile token (configure the secret in Supabase Auth as well).

# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0xPaste-site-key-here

# =============================================================================
# Server-only (NOT bundled to client) — automation scripts
# =============================================================================
#
# Personal Access Token to drive the Supabase Management API from local
# scripts (run migrations, regenerate types, etc.). No `VITE_` prefix on
# purpose: this MUST stay server-side. Generate at:
#   https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens

# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_your-personal-access-token
